{"id": "EUVD-2026-55396", "enisaUuid": "ecbc6484-0f86-3088-b4a2-1d7c4ba52dab", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: BPF: Zero-extend signed ALU32 div/mod results\n\nALU32 operations write a 32-bit result and leave the upper 32 bits of\nthe BPF register zero. The LoongArch JIT sign-extends the result of\nsigned ALU32 BPF_DIV and BPF_MOD (off=1), so a negative 32-bit quotient\nor remainder leaves bits 63:32 set in JITted code while the verifier\nand interpreter model those bits as zero.\n\nKeep sign-extension on the operands, which signed divide needs, and\nzero-extend the ALU32 result after the divide or modulo instruction,\nmatching the unsigned ALU32 div/mod paths and every other ALU32\noperation in this JIT.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:02:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:47", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7577cca85f2d4590c9d9423ba72ef54181a713c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16656c3d734693be3d8a36dbf9d09142b69f3ddc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/716cb29dbed4d62e9e108950a1a82bcba4cc2d45", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dacd348b8a993373576fe2ee2d8b114740ba57a6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-68295", "GHSA-vrqj-mf6p-p2fv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1176f07f-72f5-31ac-8ceb-76974bb9e906", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2425c9e002d2a1fdca34261b2fa6713eafef2163 <16656c3d734693be3d8a36dbf9d09142b69f3ddc"}, {"id": "690eacfe-47ee-35ea-8d63-56c43f4a336c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "9fb71777-364e-318c-b590-c0e990ea9238", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2425c9e002d2a1fdca34261b2fa6713eafef2163 <716cb29dbed4d62e9e108950a1a82bcba4cc2d45"}, {"id": "a01398d1-041f-3452-a9ce-f320cb17a3f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "c20b3d25-8d8c-337a-b312-be98e4005d60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2425c9e002d2a1fdca34261b2fa6713eafef2163 <dacd348b8a993373576fe2ee2d8b114740ba57a6"}, {"id": "c95a3c6f-3822-3d7d-b0d3-0d702a9cf72e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d5d802b1-fd05-34a8-ae3a-e9a686cd70a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "e7e0138f-2aba-3034-9b54-507385186818", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "e913a41d-8c2d-3a6d-b439-0eb65ecea7f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2425c9e002d2a1fdca34261b2fa6713eafef2163 <7577cca85f2d4590c9d9423ba72ef54181a713c9"}, {"id": "fac14fc5-3e4b-3dd2-9e3f-9cd6d1d21527", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "47609ae6-11d2-3b45-b7d2-5331a0269728", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}